{"id":"NCT06133972","title":"Phase 3 Extension Study to Evaluate Long-term Safety of Ianalumab in Participants With Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SIRIUS-SLE Extension).","official":"A Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-controlled Extension Study, Followed by a Study Treatment Withdrawal or Open-label Period, to Assess the Long-term Safety and Tolerability of Ianalumab in Patients With Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SIRIUS-SLE Extension)","summary":"The purpose of this study is to evaluate long-term safety and tolerability of ianalumab in participants with systemic lupus erythematosus who have previously completed the treatment period in one of the two SIRIUS-SLE core studies (CVAY736F12301 or CVAY736F12302).","conditions":["Systemic Lupus Erythematosus"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Placebo"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Ianalumab"}],"criteria":"Key Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Signed informed consent prior to participation in the extension study. Parent or legal guardian's signed informed consent and child's assent, if appropriate, are required before any assessment is performed for participants \\<18 years of age. Of note, if the participant reaches age of consent (age as per local law) during the study, they will also need to sign the corresponding study Informed Consent Form (ICF) at the next study visit.\n* Participants must have participated in either one of the two SIRIUS-SLE core studies, CVAY736F12301 or CVAY736F12302, and have completed the treatment period through Week 60 without treatment discontinuation.\n* In the judgement of the investigator, participants must be expected to clinically benefit from continued study treatment.\n\nKey Exclusion Criteria:\n\n* Use of prohibited therapies.\n* Active viral, bacterial or other infections requiring intravenous or intramuscular treatment for clinically significant infection which in the opinion of the investigator will place the participant at risk for participation.\n* Plans for administration of live vaccines during the study period.\n* Pregnant or nursing (lactating) women.\n\nOther protocol-defined inclusion/exclusion criteria may apply.","minAge":"12 Years","maxAge":"100 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":550,"start":"2024-05-21","pcd":"2034-04-03","upd":"2026-11-09","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","areas":["other","rare"],"central":["Novartis Pharmaceuticals · 1-888-669-6682 · novartis.email@novartis.com","Novartis Pharmaceuticals · +41613241111 · novartis.email@novartis.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Pinnacle Research Group Llc","city":"Anniston","pr":"Alabama","zip":"36207","s":"R","lat":33.6598,"lon":-85.8316,"c":"Ruby Fields · +1 256 236 0055 · rfields@pinnacletrials.com"},{"f":"Providence Medical Center","city":"Burbank","pr":"California","zip":"91505","s":"R","lat":34.1808,"lon":-118.309,"c":"Sandra Figueroa · +1 818 869 7067 · Sandra.Figueroa@providence.org"},{"f":"Advanced Medical Research","city":"La Palma","pr":"California","zip":"90623","s":"R","lat":33.8464,"lon":-118.0467,"c":"Reza Azadegan · +1 714 752 6587 · razadegan@advmedresearch.com"},{"f":"Millennium Clinical Trials","city":"Westlake Village","pr":"California","zip":"91361","s":"ANR","lat":34.1458,"lon":-118.8056,"c":""},{"f":"University of Colorado Denver","city":"Aurora","pr":"Colorado","zip":"80045","s":"R","lat":39.7294,"lon":-104.8319,"c":"Chong Pedrick · chong.pedrick@cuanschutz.edu"},{"f":"Clinical Res Of W Florida","city":"Clearwater","pr":"Florida","zip":"33765","s":"R","lat":27.9658,"lon":-82.8001,"c":"Jessica Mayfield · +1 727 466 0078 · JMayfield@crwf.com"},{"f":"GNP Research","city":"Cooper City","pr":"Florida","zip":"33024","s":"R","lat":26.0573,"lon":-80.2717,"c":"Melissa Pierce · +1 754 248 3589 · melissa@gnpresearch.com"},{"f":"Homestead Assoc In Research Inc","city":"Homestead","pr":"Florida","zip":"33033","s":"R","lat":25.4687,"lon":-80.4776,"c":"Mario Hernandez · 13052460873 · mhernandez@associatesinresearch.com"},{"f"